# The which-key popup offers the NvChad groups — +http +test +lang/run
# +integrations +insert +harpoon, the harpoon digits and the root
# leaves — and descends into them.
# (The leader tree is the vim profile's popup; the standard profile's is
# its Ctrl+K chords — `whichkey_standard_ctrl_k.test`.)
write a.txt alpha
open a.txt
command editor.use_vim
command whichkey.leader
expect screen contains "+test"
expect screen contains "+http"
expect screen contains "+lang/run"
expect screen contains "+harpoon"
expect screen contains "harpoon 1"
expect screen contains "command palette"
key T
expect screen contains "run all"
expect screen contains "flaky/wobbly dashboard"
key esc
expect screen lacks "run all"
command whichkey.leader
key t
expect screen contains "right panel"
expect screen contains "hidden files (all)"
key r
expect screen lacks "right panel"
